// TASK 4: Hash Functions
$task_contents[4] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>A Seal, Not a Lock</h2>

    <p>A cryptographic hash function takes an input of any size and produces a fixed size output called a digest. The same input always produces the same digest, and there is no key involved, so anyone can compute one.</p>

    <p>A hash is not encryption. There is no way to reverse a digest back into the original data, and there is no key to protect. Think of it as a tamper evident seal on a package rather than a lock. It proves the contents were not altered, but it does not hide them.</p>

